  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Calm Reference Sheet",
    "overview": "The site reads like a well-set reference sheet that a patient expert hands you: ruled sections, numbered entries, exact facts (DNS, diagnostics, seminar list), and real photographs of Petra at work. Competence is shown through specifics, never through intensity. Everything that could feel like a gym poster (dark drama, neon, sweat, shouting type) is absent on purpose; the audience arrives in pain or unsure whether to start, and the page lowers that fear.\n\nDensity is relaxed: one idea per section, generous vertical rhythm, a narrow reading measure. Components are calm and welcoming: flat surfaces, hairline rules, rounded pill actions, nothing that competes with the photographs. The only physical objects in the world are paper ones, a taped note and white polaroid prints, and they live in the courses section alone.\n\nLight and dark are equal citizens. Dark mode keeps the same structure on a night-teal ground; the paper objects stay light because they are prints, not UI.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Mint ground, ink text, deep teal for actions; bright mint reserved for \"now\".",
      "Hairline rules and one heavier ink rule anchoring each section's content.",
      "Numbered lists with tabular numerals instead of icon-card grids.",
      "Real photos in softly rounded frames; no illustrations standing in for the subject.",
      "Poppins throughout; Caveat handwriting only on paper objects and the story signature.",
      "Motion is an accent: one authored hero entrance, then quiet one-time fades."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Now Rule",
        "body": "Bright mint marks what is current or interactive-in-progress (active nav weight aside, selection, tape, dark-mode actions); it never becomes a large decorative field in light mode.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Band Rule",
        "body": "A page carries at most one full-width colour field. On the homepage it is the contact CTA, because contact is the site's main goal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paper Stays Paper Rule",
        "body": "Polaroids and the taped note keep the light paper colour and dark ink in both themes; links on paper use Deep Teal Ink, never the theme's primary.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hand Is Paper Rule",
        "body": "Caveat appears only on paper objects and the signature. It never sets a heading, a button or navigation.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rule Line Rule",
        "body": "Each section's content starts under a 1px ink rule; items inside are separated by 1px hairlines at 16% ink. Rules replace boxes.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Objects Cast Shadows Rule",
        "body": "If it is not paper or a floating control, it has no shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do show real photographs of Petra and real training; use the course's own photo for a course.",
      "Do structure content as ruled, numbered lists with tabular numerals before reaching for cards.",
      "Do keep every text/background pair at WCAG AA in both themes; check new colours against the mint and night grounds.",
      "Do keep motion to the hero entrance plus quiet one-time fades, and honour `prefers-reduced-motion` and no-JS.",
      "Do keep blog/GDPR pages free of Motion and form code."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use dark, intense \"gym\" imagery, neon accents or aggressive type — the audience is people in pain or just starting.",
      "Don't replace photos with illustrated body diagrams or pictograms (rejected by the owner).",
      "Don't hide content in carousels.",
      "Don't use Caveat outside paper objects and the signature.",
      "Don't put bright mint text on light grounds."
    ]
  }
}
